# ThinkPad TrackPoint on the i8042 AUX port. Newer sticks report a TrackPoint
# variant ID (0x07) the kernel driver does not accept yet, so psmouse falls
# back to "PS/2 Logitech Mouse". Tell libinput it is a pointing stick anyway.
#
# Consequence of not having this, all observed on this machine: there is no
# /sys/bus/serio/devices/serio1/sensitivity (the kernel TrackPoint driver never
# binds), and libinput applies its generic mouse acceleration curve instead of
# src/filter-trackpoint.c. niri's `input { trackpoint { } }` block is keyed on
# the same classification, so none of it reaches the device either.
#
# Ported from the Fedora side's trackpoint-config; see 72-trackpoint.ts.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="input", KERNEL=="event*", \
  ATTRS{name}=="PS/2 Logitech Mouse", \
  ATTRS{phys}=="isa0060/serio1/input0", \
  ENV{ID_INPUT_POINTINGSTICK}="1"
